{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The leading [Dm]lights of the age all wondered among [Em7b5]themselves what I would do next,
After [A7]all that I'd found, in my travels around the world, [Dm]was there anything left?
[D]"Gentlemen," I said, "I've studied the charts, and if [Gm/D]what I am thinking is right,
There's [C/E]another new world, at the top of the world, for the [F/C]first one to break through [A7/C#]the ice,"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I looked 'round the [Dm]room, in that way I once had, and I [Em7b5]saw that they wanted belief,
So I [A7]said, "All I've got are my guts and my God," then I [Dm]paused, "and the Annabel Lee."
Oh, the [Dsus]Annabel [D]Lee, I saw their eyes shine, the most [Gm]beautiful ship in the sea,
My [C]Nina, my Pinta, my Santa Maria, my beautiful [F]Annabel [A7]Lee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[Dm] [C] [Bb] [A7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
That [Dm]spring we set sail, and the crowd waved from shore, and on [Em7b5]board the sailors waved caps,
But I'd [A7]never had family, just the Annabel Lee, so I [Dm]never had cause to look back
I just [D]set the course north, studied the charts, and towards [Gm]dark I drifted toward sleep,
And I [C]dreamed of the fine, deep harbor I'd find past the [F]ice, for my Annabel [A7]Lee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
After that it got colder, and the world got [Dm]quiet. It was [Em7b5]never quite day or quite night.
And the [A7]sea turned the color of sky turned the color of [Dm]sea turned the color of ice.
Till at last [D]all around us was fastness one vast, glassy [Gm]desert of arsenic white,
And the [C]waves that once lifted us, shifted instead into [F]drifts against Annabel's [A7]sides.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
And the crew gathered [Dm]closer, at first for the warmth, but each day [Em7b5]would bring a new set
Of [A7]tracks in the snow, leading over the edge of the world, [Dm]til I was the only one left.
Then it [D]gets cloudy, But it feels like I laid there for days, [Gm]or maybe for months
But [C]Annabel held me, just the two of us happy, to [F]think back on all we had [A7]done
{end_of_verse}

